\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces \small  \textbf  {Measured laws.} A vast braid of blocks is compressed through a geometric aperture into one small proof crystal. Two verification paths leave it: the violet lane enters a laboratory instrument — \emph  {full fold verification under benchmark conditions} — while the cyan lane pulses rapid checks to a lightweight glass client — \emph  {live incremental tip verification against an already-verified state}. Along the bottom, redundant gossip routes cross a field of simulated packet loss: individual transmissions vanish, delivery survives — the $1-p^r$ law of \S  \ref {sec:delivery}. The two lanes are separate experiments, as in Figure~\ref {fig:foldflow}.}}{11}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
